# V2 — adversarial verification of the HEE v4 design documents

**Verifier:** read-only subagent, 2026-10-01 (~08:00 AEST). **Subject:** `design/ULTRAMAP.md`, `design/DEPLOYMENT_ATLAS.md`,
`design/JEV_QUESTION_RESPONSES.md`, `learnings/PROCESS-LEARNINGS.md` (all under `~/hee4-evidence/`).
**Method:** v3 read only through `git -C /run/host/var/home/herdr-engineering-engine-v3 show|grep|ls-tree b5367bc`
(`rev-parse b5367bc` = `origin/main` = `b5367bca71a4…`); evidence files read at the cited line; host probes read-only via
`flatpak-spawn --host`. No cargo, no build, no write except this file. Same-lineage verifier: this is not independent review.

## Verdict: PASS_WITH_GAPS

Facts are strong: 101 of 107 sampled claims hold. The designs disagree with each other on crate numbering, runtime paths,
the dependency checker and the phase that owns the verdict authority. Two of the ULTRAMAP's crate boundaries cannot be
enforced by the compiler as drawn.

| Document | Sampled | CONFIRMED | REFUTED | UNVERIFIABLE |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| ULTRAMAP | 34 | 32 | 2 | 0 |
| DEPLOYMENT_ATLAS | 34 | 33 | 1 | 0 |
| JEV_QUESTION_RESPONSES | 18 | 15 | 3 (line cites) | 0 |
| PROCESS-LEARNINGS | 21 | 19 | 0 | 2 |
| **Total** | **107** | **99** | **6** | **2** |

